Use the SDK compiler directly for GMP assembly inputs.

GMP probes assembler syntax even with --disable-assembly because its
cycle-counter support uses assembly. CONFIG_SITE's native C compiler wrapper
rejects the assembly-only conftest.s command with "native object compilation
requires one compiler object output". Assembly needs no C ABI lowering;
select the SDK assembler driver while retaining CONFIG_SITE for C code.

Upstream: PS5-only; separates native C ABI lowering from assembly.

--- a/depends/common/gmp/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/depends/common/gmp/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -48,6 +48,7 @@
                       BUILD_IN_SOURCE TRUE)
 else()
+  list(APPEND gmp_conf "CCAS=${CMAKE_C_COMPILER} -c")
   if(CORE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "linux" AND CPU MATCHES "i.86")
       list(APPEND gmp_conf ABI=32)
   endif()
 
